    {
      "id": "459373cf-e384-5ad2-b6e7-71a5bbcb39aa",
      "name": "Overview - read first",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -740,
        -260
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 960,
        "content": "# Prepare Whisk AI product image briefs and archive results with Google Sheets and Google Drive\n\n## Who is this for?\nE-commerce sellers and content teams who create product images manually in [Whisk AI](https://whisk-ai.io/) and need repeatable briefs, asset tracking, and review handoffs.\n\n## How it works\nThe first form collects product details, a reference-image link, and a scene preset. It prepares a prompt and records a task in Google Sheets. Open Whisk, upload your reference, and generate the image manually. Return the downloaded file through the second form with its task ID. The workflow validates the task, archives the image in Google Drive, and updates the original row. Sequential retries reuse an existing archive.\n\n## Setup\n1. Create a tracking sheet with the column names in the setup note.\n2. Connect Google Sheets and Google Drive credentials.\n3. Configure both workspace nodes and the return-form URL.\n4. Set Basic Auth credentials on both forms and test both branches.\n\n## Requirements\nn8n, Google service access, and browser access to Whisk. No Whisk API key is required. Image creation is manual; Whisk generation costs apply separately.\n\n## Customize and review\nEdit the scene prompts and upload limit. Check product shape, labels, and logos before approval. Use this with a trusted team; process returns sequentially. Create a new brief for each revision."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "a81d0664-4973-512f-8787-a04cfaabbad8",
      "name": "Setup - Google workspace",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -740,
        760
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 860,
        "content": "## One-time setup\n1. Create a Google Sheet and name its tab **Briefs**. Paste these exact column names into row 1:\n\n`brief_id | product_name | source_image_url | scene | aspect_ratio | prompt | status | created_at | drive_file_id | drive_file_url | review_notes | updated_at`\n\n2. Set the same sheet ID/tab in both **Configure ... workspace** nodes. Set the archive folder ID in the archive configuration.\n3. Connect Google Sheets credentials to all three Sheets nodes and Google Drive credentials to both Drive nodes.\n4. Set **HTTP Basic Auth credentials** on BOTH form triggers. Use this for a trusted internal team. Task IDs identify work, not people.\n5. Copy the return form Production URL into **Configure brief workspace → return_form_url**. Publish/activate only after completing setup.\n\nReference links are retained for the operator; n8n does not fetch them or send them to Whisk."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4213852a-7e70-51fd-9fd6-b26eb1e3c558",
      "name": "Prepare briefs - automatic",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -30,
        -250
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 6,
        "width": 1520,
        "height": 200,
        "content": "## 1 · Prepare and record the brief\nSubmit one product and one scene. The workflow assembles a reusable prompt and records a unique task. Google Sheets writes use RAW values. The final page links to Whisk and your configured return form.\n\nNo text-model account or Whisk API key is needed."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "bbdc95a6-7216-50ab-8f51-f1771f85db40",
      "name": "Create image - manual",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 3,
        "width": 1480,
        "height": 220,
        "content": "## 2 · Create the image manually\nOpen **[Whisk AI](https://whisk-ai.io/)** in your browser. Upload your product reference, paste the prompt, choose the ratio and generate. Download the result and submit it with the task ID in the second form.\n\nThis template does not automate Whisk or Google Labs. Whisk generation charges depend on your account and selections."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "03f9a445-3690-5eb1-a3c2-8d3518029cc4",
      "name": "Archive and review",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1510,
        340
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1740,
        "height": 230,
        "content": "## 3 · Match, archive and review\nPNG/JPEG/WebP, at most 10 MB by default. A Merge node restores the original uploaded binary after Sheets/Drive lookups. Unknown tasks and ambiguous archive matches stop before upload. Files stay in your selected folder with its existing permissions.\n\nReview in the sheet: `awaiting_creation → needs_review → approved`. For a new revision, create a new brief."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "0861061e-738e-5b4e-8bbc-bd0e9a80c3df",
      "name": "Retry behavior and limits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2640,
        1350
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 5,
        "width": 650,
        "height": 500,
        "content": "## Retry and failure handling\n- If Drive upload succeeds but updating Sheets fails, a **sequential** resubmission finds the task-prefixed filename and repairs the sheet link.\n- Keep archived filenames unchanged. The workflow checks for duplicate matches and stops for review.\n- Existing approval status and reviewer notes are preserved.\n- Concurrent submissions for the same task are not transactionally locked; submit one return at a time.\n- Google authorization/network failures are visible in n8n executions; retry after fixing the cause. No social or store publication is performed.\n- File checks validate type metadata and size, not image authenticity."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
